WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.940
Next LC-36A Tower Module Edition moves Florida Starship Operations closer to first flights. This is SpaceX Daily Episode 139, a super heavy booster heads for a whole-down firing, starship missions move in parallel, and Kennedy Space Center is asked for more land, plus the engineering deep dive. Construction crews at the historic Florida Complex are integrating the new section into the existing tower during the rebuild, according to site video on YouTube. The lift is in progress, and it falls

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.860
follows foundation and base work completed in recent weeks.

00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:38.515
Booster 22 is heading to pad 2 tonight for a potential weekend static fire test.

00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:44.015
Road delays are scheduled between 11.59 pm and 4 am central daylight time.

00:00:44.715 --> 00:00:49.415
The move puts the booster on the test stand so teams can verify propellant loading and engine

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:50.455
ignition sequences.

00:00:51.035 --> 00:00:56.295
They will watch data from all 33 Raptor engines during the planned hold-down firing, with

00:00:56.295 --> 00:00:57.815
the vehicle bolted to the stand.

00:00:57.815 --> 00:01:02.175
Any issues found feed straight into pre-flight checks for the upcoming mission.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.940
SpaceX has flight 15 targeted for mid-November from pad 2.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:13.080
Flight 16 hardware is preparing to move to Kennedy Space Center, or KSC, for a launch

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.160
from 39A.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.620
The dual flow approach lets teams ready to complete stacks at the same time.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:23.780
Booster and ship hardware for each flight follow separate processing pads at Starbase and

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:24.080
the Cape.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.740
The schedule is meant to keep both missions on track, despite shared infrastructure.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.700
Ground crews at each site are coordinating timelines to avoid resource conflicts.

00:01:34.695 --> 00:01:39.235
Kennedy Space Center is the site of a SpaceX request for more land to support advancing

00:01:39.235 --> 00:01:40.355
starship operations.

00:01:41.035 --> 00:01:46.015
The Business Journal's report, the company is asking for 400 acres that would add vehicle

00:01:46.015 --> 00:01:48.275
processing buildings and support facilities.

00:01:48.895 --> 00:01:53.735
Current KSC infrastructure is nearing capacity with multiple programs running in parallel.

00:01:53.735 --> 00:01:57.315
Well, approval would let construction start before the end of the year.

00:01:57.935 --> 00:02:02.135
The expansion lines up with earlier announcements about a higher flight cadence from the Cape.

00:02:02.998 --> 00:02:08.178
The Space Force has reassigned six national security launches to SpaceX, according to a

00:02:08.178 --> 00:02:10.158
Reddit post that remains unconfirmed.

00:02:10.638 --> 00:02:13.298
The shift came while the Vulcan rocket stays grounded.

00:02:13.938 --> 00:02:18.698
Mission Manifest now root those payloads onto Falcon 9 vehicles already in the production

00:02:18.698 --> 00:02:19.038
queue.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:24.458
you. The change increases pressure on existing booster reuse cycles at both Vandenberg and

00:02:24.458 --> 00:02:29.818
the Cape. Contract adjustments are expected to reflect the new launch dates. Space Force

00:02:29.818 --> 00:02:35.679
officials cited schedule certainty as the primary driver, unfavorable weather forced a stand

00:02:35.679 --> 00:02:41.479
down of a planned star-linked mission. SpaceX set on X. The next opportunity is no earlier

00:02:41.479 --> 00:02:47.419
than Friday, October 23. Range safety officers recorded shifting upper-level winds and lightning

00:02:47.419 --> 00:02:53.179
risk in the launch corridor. The 27 satellite stack remains secured on the pad at Vandenberg.

00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:59.344
Recovery teams will run additional checks once the window reopens. Elon Musk recommended

00:02:59.344 --> 00:03:05.044
Grockbot for almost any personal or business task. He described it as a life and business manager

00:03:05.044 --> 00:03:10.704
equivalent to having a genius employee. The recommendation points to recent gains in task handling

00:03:10.704 --> 00:03:16.484
and context retention. Follow-up posts stressed reliability for scheduling, research, and routine

00:03:16.484 --> 00:03:21.484
decisions. Early adopters report measurable time savings on repetitive workflows.

00:03:22.546 --> 00:03:26.846
Memphis is holding Musk for nights and days as the SI project fuels SpaceX

00:03:26.846 --> 00:03:31.826
expansion, the commercial appeal reports. The data center worked ties directly to

00:03:31.826 --> 00:03:35.986
revenue growth for the company. Local infrastructure upgrades are accelerating

00:03:35.986 --> 00:03:41.086
to handle higher power and cooling loads. Project timelines now include round-the-clock

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:45.266
oversight from senior leadership. Revenue from these facilities is already

00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:50.884
showing up in quarterly results reported earlier this month. Elsewhere, a Texas Environmental

00:03:50.884 --> 00:03:56.004
Review could set precedents for how SpaceX projects are assessed in Louisiana, according

00:03:56.004 --> 00:04:02.024
to the Louisiana Illuminator. XAI launched a SpaceX Super Intelligence Partner Network that

00:04:02.024 --> 00:04:07.771
connects partners to growing compute and intelligence infrastructure. Users on Reddit's SpaceX

00:04:07.771 --> 00:04:12.531
Lounge are sharing photos of Starship Mission Patch collections covering every flight test

00:04:12.531 --> 00:04:17.991
through flight 14. Those collections mix official SpaceX patches with NASA Space Flight

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:22.731
editions obtained when shipping costs were lower. Community members on X are trying

00:04:22.731 --> 00:04:27.391
Grockbot for daily scheduling and research and reporting quick replies on both personal

00:04:27.391 --> 00:04:32.849
and technical questions. Worth keeping an eye on is a Houston Chronicle opinion arguing

00:04:32.849 --> 00:04:38.429
that Boca Chica State Parkland should remain public. The column tells Elon Musk the state will

00:04:38.429 --> 00:04:43.329
not simply hand that acreage over. It frames the talks as a test of whether private space

00:04:43.329 --> 00:04:47.909
development can override established public access rights without stronger environmental

00:04:47.909 --> 00:04:53.689
and community safeguards. Resolution would take either legislation or a negotiated settlement

00:04:53.689 --> 00:04:57.729
that satisfies both park advocates and SpaceX infrastructure needs.

00:04:58.449 --> 00:05:03.249
Local stakeholders keep pressing for more studies on habitat and public recreation impacts

00:05:03.249 --> 00:05:09.801
before any transfer proceeds. Starship propellant from an engineering standpoint only beats Falcon 9

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:17.601
economics after the vehicle reaches high flight rates. A full stack holds roughly 4,600 to 5,100 tons

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:25.641
of propellant. One Falcon 9 tanks about 490 to 515 tons, so 10 of those flights burn a similar mass.

00:05:26.261 --> 00:05:32.441
One half loaded Starship on flight 14 already equaled the work of about 10 Falcon 9 V2 mini-flights,

00:05:32.441 --> 00:05:38.241
carrying 26 V3 Starlink satellites rated at roughly 1 terabit per second a piece.

00:05:38.661 --> 00:05:43.821
At full load, the gap widens, because both stages are designed to fly again, and the vehicle

00:05:43.821 --> 00:05:48.321
can put up to 20 times Falcon 9's orbital mass on a comparable propellant burn.

00:05:48.961 --> 00:05:53.541
Reuse spreads the same tanks and fuel over many flights, until the rate is high.

00:05:54.041 --> 00:05:56.301
Those tons do not yet mean cheaper satellites.

00:05:56.941 --> 00:06:02.261
Oxygen and methane are liquefied from electricity and feedstock, so cost per ton tracks

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:07.901
power price and plant hours, not scarce ore. A back-of-envelope figure for air separation

00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:13.821
is on the order of 0.4 to 1 kilowatt hour per kilogram of liquid oxygen, with methane

00:06:13.821 --> 00:06:19.681
via hydrogen adding more through electrolysis. Kinetic energy to low-earth orbit is about 30

00:06:19.681 --> 00:06:25.261
megajoules per kilogram. Gravity and drag mean the chemical energy you burn is several times that,

00:06:25.641 --> 00:06:31.521
which is why the tanks dwarf the payload. The rocket equation is unforgiving. Most of the propellant

00:06:31.521 --> 00:06:36.121
exists to lift the rest of the propellant, so throwing stages away multiplies the metal

00:06:36.121 --> 00:06:36.841
you pay for.

00:06:37.261 --> 00:06:42.541
Ten Falcon 9 flights spread that energy across ten vehicles and ten ground crews, while

00:06:42.541 --> 00:06:46.101
one starship flight pours it into a single stack and a single pad.

00:06:46.741 --> 00:06:52.161
Once the super heavy booster and the ship both return and fly again within days, tower, pad,

00:06:52.401 --> 00:06:54.841
and factory stop dominating the per flight bill.

00:06:55.341 --> 00:06:59.621
On a generic rocket, dry structure might be on the order of a tenth of the fueled mass,

00:06:59.621 --> 00:07:05.061
fast, discard it, and you buy a new 10th every flight, but fly that metal 100 times and

00:07:05.061 --> 00:07:08.701
a back-of-envelope split puts the structure near 1% per flight.

00:07:09.241 --> 00:07:10.941
That is the idiot index in launch.

00:07:11.541 --> 00:07:15.781
The finished satellite costs many times the raw propellant and metal because expendable

00:07:15.781 --> 00:07:16.921
hardware ate the money.

00:07:17.541 --> 00:07:19.921
A rough estimate is tens of times those inputs.

00:07:20.581 --> 00:07:25.741
Starship drives that ratio down by reusing both stages and flying often enough that overhead

00:07:25.741 --> 00:07:27.041
per flight becomes small.

00:07:27.041 --> 00:07:33.341
When one stack flies as many times in a year as 10 Falcon 9 boosters combined, the propellant

00:07:33.341 --> 00:07:36.641
math becomes a lower cost for every kilogram placed in orbit.

00:07:37.221 --> 00:07:39.661
The stock was trading higher, up 2%.

00:07:39.661 --> 00:07:45.713
Before we go, if tonight's road closure holds, booster 22 could be on the pad to stand

00:07:45.713 --> 00:07:47.133
for a weekend static fire.

